# Z.AI Rules

Z.AI (GLM) at **GLM Coding Plan** base URL `https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4`.

## Model table

|| Cursor alias    | Real model       | Description                                                         ||
|| --------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- ||
|| `gpt-4.1-turbo` | `glm-5.3[1m]`    | 1M context flagship; always thinks; reasoning_effort + prompt cache  ||
|| `gpt-4.1`       | `glm-4.7`        | Budget workhorse; thinking on/off only                             ||
|| (internal)      | `glm-4.6v`       | **Vision worker** only — describes images for ALL providers. Not user-selectable; not in `/v1/models`. Runs on the coding-plan endpoint. ||

`glm-4.6v` has **no Cursor alias**. Invoked by `vision.Describer`; usage bills under `zai::glm-4.6v`.

## API key

- Key field: `zaiKeyEncrypted` in `config.AppSettings`
- Set via: `discursive set --zai-key <key>`
- Retrieved via: `settings.GetZaiKey(dataRoot)`

## Pricing (USD per 1M tokens)

Source: https://docs.z.ai/guides/overview/pricing

|| Model     | Cache hit | Cache miss | Output ||
|| --------- | --------- | ---------- | ------ ||
|| `glm-5.3` | $0.26     | $1.40      | $4.40  ||
|| `glm-4.7` | $0.11     | $0.60      | $2.20  ||

> **GLM Coding Plan billing is points-based**, not per-token. The USD/MTok
> table above converts multipliers (input 6.9, cached input 1.7, output 24 per 10k
> tokens) at 1 USD = 10 points. Actual spend tracks plan credits; use this
> table for estimation only. Peak/off-peak multipliers apply (off-peak = 50%).

## Sanitizer policy

|| Model     | Parameter          | Action                                                                                                                                                             ||
|| --------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ ||
|| `glm-5.3` | `thinking`         | Always `{type: "enabled"}` — `disabled` is **not supported** and fails upstream                                                                                    ||
|| `glm-5.3` | `reasoning_effort` | Always sent, `low`\|`high`\|`max`. Normalized via `normalizeZaiEffort()` → `off`/`none`/`minimal`↦`low`, `medium`↦`high`, `xhigh`↦`max`, `high`/`max` pass-through ||
|| `glm-4.7` | `thinking`         | Set `{type: "enabled"\|"disabled"}` (toggle, live `ThinkingEnabled` map); no reasoning_effort support                                                              ||
|| `glm-4.7` | `reasoning_effort` | Deleted                                                                                                                                                            ||

The thinking-toggle set is a whitelist (`zaiThinkingToggle()`): `glm-4.7` only.
Apply `PolicyZai` case in `applyThinkingPolicy()` and `stripUnsupportedParams()`.

## Reasoning effort normalization (Z.AI-specific)

`glm-5.3` always thinks — thinking cannot be disabled upstream, so the minimum
effort level is `low`. The gateway normalizes effort via `normalizeZaiEffort()`
to the values the catalog advertises (`low`, `high`, `max` are ever sent):

|| UI label    | Sent to Z.AI                                         ||
|| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- ||
|| Off / None  | `low` (minimum thinking — `disabled` is unsupported) ||
|| Low         | `low`                                                ||
|| Medium      | `high`                                               ||
|| High        | `high`                                               ||
|| XHigh / Max | `max`                                                ||

The `ReasoningEffortCatalog` entry for `glm-5.3` advertises: `low`, `high`, `max`
and defaults to `low` (cost-conscious, mirroring Kimi K3).
`glm-4.7` does not appear in the catalog (no effort selection).

