## Plan concurrency (hard routing)

The GLM Coding Plan allows ~2 concurrent requests upstream. The gateway does
**not** enforce a local semaphore or overflow to other providers (removed 2026-08).

- **Chat**: requests go to the resolved Z.AI model; HTTP 429 →
  `doUpstreamWithRetry()` (3×, 250/500/1000ms backoff).
- **Router downgrades**: within Z.AI only (`glm-5.3` → `glm-4.7`).
- **Vision**: `config.VisionModelFor(ProviderZai)` → `glm-4.6v` for Z.AI-routed
  requests; other providers use their own vision models.

Plan capacity is an upstream constraint — reduce parallel Z.AI load or accept
429 retries; no cross-provider overflow.

